    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:936a34ccc6e7c635",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "b33e176f29c01a8e8c7bbb17f2d2dc2fd64936eb0d2ad0bd0740e401e7efda89",
      "text": "Day 14 · Breakfast. Free day for walks or optional excursions (see Optional Excursions).\n\nBotanical Garden\n\nRio de Janeiro · Day 14 · 4 hours\n\nPrice on request\n\nA garden more than 200 years old, with thousands of plant species, orchids, bromeliads and the pond of giant water lilies, in the shadow of Corcovado.\n\nImperial Petrópolis\n\nRio de Janeiro · Day 14\n\nPrice on request\n\nThe historic mountain town 60 km from Rio: the Imperial Museum, with the crown of Emperor Pedro II, and the Gothic Cathedral, where the emperor, his wife and Princess Isabel are buried.\n\nSamba show\n\nRio de Janeiro · 4 hours\n\nPrice on request\n\nDinner included\n\nAn evening of Brazilian music and dance, samba and capoeira, with dinner during the show.\n\nHelicopter over Rio\n\nFrom Sugar Loaf or Lagoa · 8–9 min\n\nPrice on request\n\nChrist the Redeemer, Sugar Loaf, Two Brothers and the curves of Copacabana and Ipanema from the sky.",
